# Reference only - Hermes reads its real .env from ~/Hermes/.env, NOT from this project folder.
# The web UI's Setup screen writes GEMINI_API_KEY for you (paste your key, click "Test & save key").
# To set it up by hand instead, create ~/Hermes/.env with this content:
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key-here

# Hermes is model-agnostic (via LiteLLM). LLM_MODEL picks the model/provider; its default is Gemini.
# To switch providers, change LLM_MODEL to that provider's litellm model string and put ITS OWN key
# in this file too (e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY for "gpt-4o"). See https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/providers
# LLM_MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.1-pro-preview
